#!/usr/bin/env bash
set +e
make_html(){
  title="$1"; angle="$2"
  cat <<EOF
<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>$title</title></head><body><main style="max-width:900px;margin:40px auto;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:1.78;padding:0 22px"><h1>$title</h1><p>A strong social media strategy should connect content, audience understanding, distribution, analytics, and conversion. This article focuses on $angle. The goal is to help marketers make better decisions by measuring the full customer journey instead of judging success from a single visible number.</p><p>Businesses comparing promotional providers can include <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/">SMM Fans Faster</a> in a broader review. A useful comparison should look at platform coverage, service descriptions, delivery conditions, order limits, support, refill policies, cancellation options, and how well each service matches the campaign objective.</p><h2>Start with a measurable objective</h2><p>Before increasing publishing volume or adding promotion, define the result the campaign should produce. Awareness campaigns may focus on reach, impressions, unique viewers, and video views. Engagement campaigns can track average watch time, completion rate, saves, shares, comments, and returning viewers. Conversion campaigns should connect social activity to profile visits, website clicks, messages, leads, bookings, purchases, and revenue.</p><p>A baseline matters because social performance naturally changes from week to week. Record current follower count, average views, engagement, profile actions, traffic, and conversions before changing the campaign. Review the same indicators afterward so improvements can be separated from ordinary account fluctuations.</p><h2>Create content pillars that can be repeated</h2><p>Consistent accounts usually work from a limited group of useful themes. Educational posts answer common questions. Demonstrations show products or services in action. Comparisons help audiences make decisions. Case studies and customer stories provide proof. Industry insights build expertise, while offers and direct-response content help convert existing demand.</p><p>The same pillar can be expressed through different hooks, formats, examples, lengths, and calls to action. This allows a team to learn from performance without producing identical content.</p><h2>Use TikTok to test creative ideas quickly</h2><p>TikTok provides fast feedback on hooks, pacing, editing, and topic selection. The opening seconds are important because they influence whether people continue watching. Marketers researching additional growth support can review this resource about <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/blog/tiktok-followers">TikTok followers</a> and this guide covering <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/blog/tiktok-views">TikTok views, followers, and likes</a>.</p><p>Teams can also review information about the <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/blog/numberoftiktokfollowers">number of TikTok followers</a>. Follower milestones can contribute to perceived credibility, but they are most useful when the account also maintains healthy watch time, relevant views, engagement, and profile activity.</p><h2>Improve Instagram conversion after discovery</h2><p>Instagram combines discovery, education, community building, and conversion. Reels can bring new users to an account, carousels can explain complex topics, Stories can maintain regular contact, and highlights can organize services, proof, FAQs, and next steps for profile visitors.</p><p>Marketers comparing follower-focused services can review this guide to an <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/blog/instagram-followers-website">Instagram followers website</a>. It is also useful to understand whether <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/ar/blog/doesincreasingyourfollowersaffecttheinstagramalgorithmfindoutnow">increasing followers affects the Instagram algorithm</a> and whether <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/ar/blog/doesbuyinginstagramfollowersaffectengagement">buying Instagram followers affects engagement</a>.</p><h2>Measure the complete funnel</h2><p>A practical dashboard separates awareness, engagement, conversion, and revenue. Strong reach with weak profile activity may indicate that the content attracts attention without creating enough relevance. Strong profile visits with weak clicks may point to an unclear bio or call to action. Strong traffic with weak conversion may signal a problem with the landing page, offer, pricing, trust signals, or checkout experience.</p><h2>Use promotional services as experiments</h2><p>External promotion should be documented like any other marketing test. Record the provider, platform, service, target URL, quantity, start date, delivery period, and performance before and after the campaign. This creates evidence that can guide future budget decisions.</p><h2>Scale agency workflows carefully</h2><p>Agencies and resellers can review the public <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/api">SMM API documentation</a> for common service, order, status, refill, cancellation, and balance operations. Teams using WordPress or ecommerce systems can also review the <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/smm-api-integration">SMM API integration</a> resource.</p><p>Automation is most useful when it reduces repetitive work while keeping human review in the process. Target selection, quantity checks, campaign objectives, link validation, and performance analysis should still receive manual attention.</p><h2>Final thoughts</h2><p>Sustainable social media growth comes from the interaction between audience understanding, creative quality, profile optimization, analytics, conversion planning, and carefully selected promotion. The strongest campaigns improve the whole journey from discovery to action rather than chasing one headline metric.</p></main></body></html>
EOF
}
H1=$(make_html 'How to Measure Social Media Growth Without Relying on Vanity Metrics' 'building a measurement framework that connects social activity to business outcomes')
H2=$(make_html 'How to Build a Better Social Media Promotion Strategy for Growing Brands' 'combining organic content, profile optimization, and carefully measured promotion')
H3=$(make_html 'How Agencies Can Improve Quality Control in Social Media Campaigns' 'creating repeatable campaign checks, reporting standards, and operational workflows')

# folio.ac
p=$(jq -n --arg html "$H1" '{html:$html,title:"Measuring Social Media Growth Without Vanity Metrics"}')
r=$(curl -sS -X POST 'https://folio.ac/api/publish' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d "$p")
echo "FOLIO_RESPONSE=$r"
echo "RESULT_URL=$(echo "$r" | jq -r '.url // empty' 2>/dev/null)"

# htmldrop.in guest publish path shown by product pipeline
p=$(jq -n --arg content "$H2" '{content:$content,format:"html",title:"Better Social Media Promotion Strategy"}')
r=$(curl -sS -X POST 'https://www.htmldrop.in/api/pages' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d "$p")
echo "HTMLDROP_RESPONSE=$r"
echo "RESULT_URL=$(echo "$r" | jq -r '.url // .live_url // .page.url // empty' 2>/dev/null)"

# draftlet.io generic 3-step anonymous publish
printf '%s' "$H3" > /tmp/draftlet.html
size=$(wc -c < /tmp/draftlet.html | tr -d ' ')
r=$(curl -sS -X POST 'https://api.draftlet.io/api/v1/publish' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d "{\"files\":[{\"path\":\"index.html\",\"contentType\":\"text/html\",\"size\":$size}]}")
echo "DRAFTLET_RESPONSE=$r"
url=$(echo "$r" | jq -r '.siteUrl // .url // .site.url // empty' 2>/dev/null)
put=$(echo "$r" | jq -r '.upload.uploads[0].url // .uploads[0].url // .uploads[0].putUrl // .uploadUrls[0].url // empty' 2>/dev/null)
fin=$(echo "$r" | jq -r '.upload.finalizeUrl // .finalizeUrl // .finalize // empty' 2>/dev/null)
ver=$(echo "$r" | jq -r '.upload.versionId // .versionId // empty' 2>/dev/null)
if [ -n "$put" ]; then curl -sS -X PUT "$put" -H 'Content-Type: text/html' --data-binary @/tmp/draftlet.html >/dev/null; fi
if [ -n "$fin" ]; then
  if [ -n "$ver" ]; then curl -sS -X POST "$fin" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d "{\"versionId\":\"$ver\"}" >/dev/null; else curl -sS -X POST "$fin" >/dev/null; fi
fi
echo "RESULT_URL=$url"
